# Frontend Rules — Pocket Portfolio

## Theme & Design System
- **Primary palette:** White backgrounds, green accents (#16a34a / green-600 for primary actions, #15803d / green-700 for hover). Use emerald scale for variety.
- **Neutral palette:** Slate grays (slate-50 through slate-900) for text and borders.
- **Accent colors:** Red-500 for losses/negative, green-500 for gains/positive, amber-500 for warnings.
- **Typography:** Use Inter (sans-serif) via `next/font`. Font sizes follow Tailwind defaults.
- **Spacing:** Consistent 4px grid (p-1 = 4px, p-2 = 8px, etc.)
- **Border radius:** Rounded-lg (8px) for cards, rounded-md (6px) for buttons and inputs.
- **Shadows:** Use shadow-sm for cards, shadow-md for dropdowns/modals.

## Component Patterns

### Server Components (default)
```tsx
// src/app/(dashboard)/portfolio/page.tsx
import { getPortfolios } from "@/server/dal/portfolios";
import { PortfolioList } from "@/components/dashboard/portfolio-list";

export default async function PortfolioPage() {
  const portfolios = await getPortfolios();
  return <PortfolioList portfolios={portfolios} />;
}
```

### Client Components (only when needed)
```tsx
// src/components/forms/add-holding-form.tsx
"use client";

import { useState } from "react";
import { useAction } from "next-safe-action/hooks";
import { addHolding } from "@/server/actions/holdings";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";

export function AddHoldingForm({ accountId }: { accountId: string }) {
  // Interactive form logic here
}
```

## Dashboard Layout Rules
- Sidebar navigation on the left (collapsible on mobile)
- Top header with user avatar (Clerk UserButton), household selector, notification area
- Main content area with max-width container (max-w-7xl)
- Use Tremor Grid and Col components for dashboard card layouts
- KPI cards at the top of dashboard pages (total net worth, day change, total gain/loss)
- Charts below KPI cards, tables below charts

## Currency Display Rules
- Always format with `formatCurrency()` from `lib/utils.ts`
- Input: integer cents → Output: "$1,234.56"
- Gains: green text with "+" prefix and up arrow icon
- Losses: red text with "−" prefix and down arrow icon
- Percentages: always show 2 decimal places
- Large numbers: use abbreviations on mobile (1.2M, 45.3K) but full numbers on desktop

## Table Patterns
- Use shadcn/ui DataTable with TanStack Table for sortable, filterable data
- Always include: column sorting, search/filter, pagination (25 rows default)
- Holdings tables must show: ticker, name, shares, avg cost, current price, market value, gain/loss ($), gain/loss (%), custodian
- Use sticky headers on scroll
- Row click navigates to detail view

## Form Patterns
- Use React Hook Form + Zod resolver for all forms
- Show inline validation errors below fields (red-500 text, text-sm)
- Submit buttons show loading spinner during Server Action execution
- Success: toast notification (sonner) + redirect or data refresh
- Error: toast notification with error message
- All monetary inputs accept decimal format (user types "150.50"), convert to cents on submit

## Chart Patterns
- Portfolio value over time: Tremor AreaChart with green gradient fill
- Asset allocation: Tremor DonutChart with custom color palette
- Holdings performance: Recharts BarChart (green for positive, red for negative)
- Use Lightweight Charts (TradingView) for stock price detail views with candlestick option

## Loading & Error States
- Every route has a `loading.tsx` with skeleton matching the page layout
- Every route has an `error.tsx` with friendly error message and retry button
- Use Suspense boundaries around data-fetching sections within pages
- Empty states: illustration + descriptive text + CTA button (e.g., "Add your first holding")

## Accessibility
- All interactive elements must be keyboard navigable
- Use semantic HTML (nav, main, section, article, header)
- ARIA labels on icon-only buttons
- Color is never the only indicator (always pair with icon or text)
- Minimum touch targets: 44x44px on mobile
